    "created_at": "2018-08-20T18:00:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-20T18:00:34Z",
    "body": "So, you actually want to revert #201, #231 and #232 and give the control over transparent proxies to developers?\r\n\r\nNote that Gecko has a LOAD_BYPASS_LOCAL_CACHE flag [1].  Setting that flag will bypass opening the local cache entry and won't set any Cache-control request headers.  But, will also refresh DNS (not sure why this has been designed that way..)\r\n\r\n\r\n[1] https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/847b64cc28b74b44c379f9bff4f415b97da1c6d7/netwerk/base/nsICachingChannel.idl#96-101",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
